munication. 2021;6: 13–13. doi: 10.3389/fcomm.2021.588823 [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n* 41.Kessler G, Ye Hee Lee M. President Trump’s first 100 days: The fact check tally. The Washington Post. 2017. Available: https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/fact-checker/wp/2017/05/01/president-trumps-first-100-days-the-fact-check-tally/ [Google Scholar]\n* 42.Kessler G. About the fact checker. The Washington Post. 2017. Available: https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2019/01/07/about-fact-checker/ [Google Scholar]\n* 43.Serota KB, Levine TR, Boster FJ. The prevalence of lying in America: Three studies of self-reported lies. Human Communication Research. 2010;36: 2–25. doi: 10.1111/j.1468-2958.2009.01366.x [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n* 44.Daiku Y, Serota KB, Levine TR. A few prolific liars in Japan: Replication and the effects of Dark Triad personality traits. PLOS ONE. 2021;16: e0249815–e0249815. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0249815 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n* 45.Serota KB, Levine TR. A few prolific liars: Variation in the prevalence of lying. Journal of Language and Social Psychology. 2015;34: 138–157. doi: 10.1177/0261927x14528804 [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n* 46.Markowitz DM. Toward a deeper understanding of prolific lying: Building a profile of situation-level and individual-level characteristics. Communication Research. 2023;50: 80–105. doi: 10.1177/00936502221097041 [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n* 47.Serota KB, Levine TR, Docan-Morgan T. Unpacking variation in lie prevalence: Prolific liars, bad lie days, or both? Communication Monographs. 2021. doi: 10.1080/03637751.2021.1985153/SUPPL\\_FILE/RCMM\\_A\\_1985153\\_SM5737.DOCX [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n* 48.Graves L. Anatomy of a Fact Check: Objective Practice and the Contested Epistemology of Fact Checking. Communication, Culture & Critique. 2017;10: 518–537. doi: 10.1111/cccr.12163 [DOI] [Google Scholar]\n\n## Associated Data\n\nThis section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article.\n\n### Supplementary Materials\n\n### Data Availability Statement\n\nThe data were acquired from The Washington Post upon agreement that they would not be shared publicly. The authors will make data available to researchers upon reasonable request, or they can contact Glenn Kessler — maintainer of the Fact Checker — at The Washington Post directly for the data (Glenn.Kessler@washpost.com).","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":8088.3725590247195,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}